    "question": "An enterprise company wants to allow its developers to purchase third-party software through AWS Marketplace. The company uses an AWS Organizations account structure with full features enabled, and has a shared services account in each organizational unit (OU) that will be used by procurement managers. The procurement team’s policy indicates that developers should be able to obtain third-party software from an approved list only and use Private Marketplace in AWS Marketplace to achieve this requirement. The procurement team wants administration of Private Marketplace to be restricted to a role named procurement-manager-role, which could be assumed by procurement managers. Other IAM users, groups, roles, and account administrators in the company should be denied Private Marketplace administrative access. What is the MOST e cient way to design an architecture to meet these requirements?",
    "question_zh": "一家企业公司希望允许其开发人员透过AWS Marketplace 购买第三方软体。该公司使用启用了全部功能的 AWS Organizations ​​帐户结构，并在每个组织单位 (OU) 中拥有一个供采购经理使用的共享服务帐户。采购团队的政策表明，开发者应该只能从批准的清单中获取第三方软体，并使用AWS Marketplace中的Private Marketplace来实现这一要求。采购团队希望私人市场的管理仅限于名为采购经理角色的角色，该角色可以由采购经理承担。公司中的其他 IAM 使用者、群组、角色和帐户管理员应被拒绝 Private Marketplace 管理存取权限。设计架构以满足这些要求的最有效方法是什么？",
